00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.310 align:start position:0%
with the handover of stolen and looted  art works in the news European ministers  are sent to discuss proposals for new  rules on the return of cultural objects  unlawfully removed from a member state  the aim of the proposals is to ensure  that any national treasures such as art  or archaeological findings are swiftly  and efficiently returned to their  country of origin to this purpose they  broaden the definition of national  treasures extend return deadlines and  place the burden of proof on the  possessor of the works of art when it  comes to compensation at the meeting in  Brussels the council will also address  media freedom and pluralism which the EU  considers to be one of the pillars of  democracy there are three key issues  transparency of media ownership ensuring  that journalists are free from political  influence and that their sources are  protected and the independence of  audio-visual regulators The ministers  will also hold a public debate on the  issue of governance in sport their talks  at a focus on the framework and culture  influencing the way that a sports body  sets up its policy and rules monitors  performance handles risk and reports on  its activities good governance in sport  is an increasingly important issue and  is considered to be a precondition for  self-regulation by sports organizations
 

